          <div class="math-bio">&#956;N adds new susceptibles (births) every day, exactly balancing &#956;S removed by mortality. S is continuously replenished — the disease never runs out of fuel.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="expl-box orange">
          <h4>Why the disease persists</h4>
          <p>Births produce new susceptible individuals (unvaccinated newborns) at rate &#956;N per day. These refill S back to the threshold 1/R&#8320;. The disease circulates at equilibrium I* — never exploding (not enough fuel) and never dying (always enough fuel).</p>
