<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4 — I* AND S*
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="sec-head" id="sec-istar">
  <div class="sec-num">4</div>
  <h2>I* and S* — The Endemic Equilibrium Explained</h2>
  <p>At equilibrium, births exactly replenish what infections consume, and recoveries exactly match new infections. These balance conditions uniquely determine \(S^*\) and \(I^*\).</p>
</div>

